From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:20:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: AP MLD: remove a link only when it is on the list

hostapd_bss_link_deinit() takes hapd->started to mean that the BSS is
linked. hostapd_setup_bss() sets it before the link joins the MLD, so a
setup that fails in between, for example in hostapd_drv_link_add(),
reaches hostapd_mld_remove_link() with a node that was never added.
dl_list_del() then dereferences NULL. The failure paths of
hostapd_add_iface(), hostapd_setup_interface_complete_sync() and the
ucode iface.add_bss() have this exposure, and so does a stop of the
first BSS through the ucode bss.stop() followed by its deinit, which
removes the same node twice.

dl_list_del() clears the node and a BSS is allocated zeroed, so
hapd->link.next is NULL exactly when the node is on no list.
hostapd_mld_remove_link() now removes a node only when it is on the
list.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -5436,6 +5436,9 @@ int hostapd_mld_remove_link(struct hosta
 	if (!mld)
 		return -1;
 
+	if (!hapd->link.next)
+		return 0;
+
 	dl_list_del(&hapd->link);
 	mld->num_links--;
 
